.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sign 1  "sign " 
.SH NAME
sign \- Sign HTML blocks matching a CSS selector
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsign\fR [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find every element matching SELECTOR (full CSS selectors, e.g.
div.text, #price, article[data\-id="42"]), remove any existing
data\-hs\-signature, sign the SHA3\-256 digest of the block\*(Aqs canonical
serialization — whitespace\-normalized so signatures survive server\-side
minification — and inject the new signature attribute.
.PP
The output is written to \-\-output, or back over FILE in place. The secret
key defaults to ~/.local/share/hs/keys/default.hskey (override with \-k);
its passphrase is prompted unless \-\-no\-passphrase or \-\-passphrase\-file is
given.
.PP
A block that already sits inside another signed block is skipped (it is
covered by the enclosing signature); skipped blocks are reported and left
untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Path to the secret key file (.hskey)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR
Use an empty passphrase (no prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fI<PASSPHRASE_FILE>\fR
Read the passphrase from a file (first line)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output HTML file path (default: overwrite FILE)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
HTML file to sign
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
CSS selector of the block(s) to sign
